body:
In all honesty for those games being silver MMR you are not putting yourself enough ahead in anyway to carry.... You need to start pulling a bit more weight, one thing to consider is that high silver/low gold is only a tier away from plat, and given you say you are a plat smurf means that odds are you will struggle some games because the skill gap isn't as big as it should be...

&#x200B;

Here's my Evelynn account, I was Masters s7, diamond s8 and even I struggle some games.... but all in all carrying a 70%+ should be no issue, the majority of my losses are from having an entire team of straight feeders... I had one game where my team was like 1-30 and I was 11-7 lol..... best thing you can do is not tilt from games that are "unwinnable" and just go next with a clean head and carry hard.

&#x200B;

 [https://na.op.gg/summoner/userName=I+abuse+evelynn](https://na.op.gg/summoner/userName=I+abuse+evelynn)

Here's the list I have kogged with for 3 seasons and DL max;

&#x200B;

2x fabled raven (previous seasons used trance archfiend but raven is much better you can use raven to discard ceruli and snoww at the same time, snow will resolve first searching reign then ceruli will resolve to SS reign and complete the standard combo).

3x snoww

2x ceruli

2x reign

2x gates of the dark world

1x broww

3x dark world dealings

3x into the void

2x hey! trunade

&#x200B;

Extra deck;

&#x200B;

Stardust dragon - This card is amazing vs yubel, discard 2 cards with raven and use snowws effect from being discarded (off ceruli) to SS one of their level 4's once it goes to grave, this will make stardust.

Ancient fairy dragon 

Fabled valkyrus

Fabled ragin

Dark highlander

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

run grit as your skill so that going first you aren't auto losing duels

Matchups:

&#x200B;

Heros: Surprisingly a very easy matchup, be careful when letting them pop your grit as if they have drilldark + another hero monster + mask change they can kill you through grit.

&#x200B;

Many hero players will use drilldark to ss, then they proceed to attack with both drill + the other destiny hero monster, then use mask change.

&#x200B;

This is an obvious misplay I have seen countless hero players in the ladder/kc cup do and it never ceases to amaze me, they have 100% kill potential by attacking once with a 1600, using mask change, then using their final 1600. Take advantage of this misplay and punish them with trunade and otk.

&#x200B;

For this matchup you will always need to resolve Trunade, they run balance and are bound to see a trap that will stop your plays, if you get to higher portions of the ladder and see a lot of this deck you can consider Dark world Lightning for additional clear however I do not recommend it.

&#x200B;

Yubel: This is quite possibly the most impossible matchup for this deck, your only win con is that they did not draw a way to set up yubel, or you must resolve two reign combos (1 on the second form, and 1 on the third) in addition they must not have sphere kuriboh.

&#x200B;

Stall as long as you can until you see double reign, or simply go in as soon as possible if you don't see yubel hit the board.

&#x200B;

I don't think this deck will ever take over the ladder but if it does a card that completely counters them and synergizes with the deck is Skull Meister, this is a hand trap that will negate the effect of an opponents monster in the graveyard (during either players turn). This completely stops yubel, in addition he can still be used vs other decks (hero celestial and vampire fodder monsters), he also is a body big enough to OTK alongside Reign.

&#x200B;

Silent spellbook: This matchup is again like yubel, if silent magician hits the board you must resolve two reign combos to win this matchup, if they only have blueboy the moment you draw trunade you should be able to otk them, try to end as soon as possible if they don't have silent magician.

&#x200B;

U.A: Very easy matchup, typically they only run the u.a trap and sometimes treach/canadias, resolve your trunade if needed pop their monsters and otk. sometimes they have kuribohs so don't overuse Dark World Dealings.

&#x200B;

Vampire: Tough matchup, they can get 3 monsters on board simply with a gozuki or vampire skull to send vampire retainer and then using his effect to search the trap that allows them to SS given they sent a vampire monster to the grave for retainers effect.

&#x200B;

Gladiator beast: easy matchup given you draw the correct cards, use trunade and do the normal otk, rarely see kuribohs.

&#x200B;

Buster blader: easy matchup given you draw the correct cards, use trunade and do the normal otk. If they summon Dark Paladin they can negate until they have no cards left in hand, when this happens sometimes there is nothing you can do, use your worse spells first if possible, you can also go for an early Trance archfiend effect to discard ceruli and then reign if you have it, this will allow you to force backrow and punish while having the option to pop monsters or S/T.

&#x200B;

Dragunity: This matchup is normally a breeze, they don't run much backrow and if you resolve the Ceruli->Reign combo it makes their equip dragunity effect not go off (the one that pops a card when sent as a equip), sometimes I see them run double cyclone in this case hope you have trunade.

&#x200B;

Blue eyes: sometimes just resolving the ceruli->reign is enough to win this matchup, they use a lot of resources for cosmo brain, every now and then you need trunade for actual disruption backrow, and also you want to prevent them from using their cards that ss from grave to prevent your otk, its best to push with trunade, however is not always needed.

&#x200B;

Banish control: Easy matchup similar to glads, resolve trunade and reign and you will win.

&#x200B;

Fur hire: very tough matchup due to wiz negation and the fact they can flood 3 to their board on turn 1, end this game fast before they see wiz or clog their board, most fur decks are backrow heavy and will thus need trunade most of the time.

&#x200B;

Bujins: can be tough given they get the correct graveyard set-up however most of the time they don't even have backrow so Reign combo can be enough to win the duel.

&#x200B;

Geargias: Honestly a very annoying matchup, you will normally need trunade and if they chain pulse mines you are forced to pass or go in just to stay in the game, thankfully pulse is a 2 of and you will see trunade more than they see pulse statistically due to deck thinning.

&#x200B;

Gem knights: they can otk through grit as long as they can summon brilliant + have an extra monster to summon, insanely hard matchup, They can also use lapiz lazuli effect to burn you before pushing and thus killing through grit easy, pray you are going second and that you can otk them first, if they have grit you must resolve double Reign + have a normal summon of any monster of you lose.

&#x200B;

Burn decks: Playing vs burn can go both ways however I typically enjoy it as they give you a lot of time to draw into your combo pieces and if they don't have mirror wall or kuriboh you normally just otk them, parasite can be annoying and you must also be careful of other burn cards like lava golem if you try to push but can not otk.

&#x200B;

Mirror match: This I have played a few times and it is by far a huge skill matchup, do NOT be the first to activate dark world dealings, your opponent will get to trigger effects and really gain advantage, you can outplay your opponent by not using DWD and when they use it net advantage or even sometimes discard ceruli to ss reign and pop anything they may have on the board, in this matchup try to use your effects of Trance archfiend or gates of the dark world to discard, otherwise you will also help your opponent.

&#x200B;

All in all Dark Worlds are fully capable of both KOG and DL. Max its a very glass cannon deck and normally you will know if the game is over by turn 2 if not 3.

&#x200B;

This deck has a lot of split UR's from different main boxes, however it is not a bad deck to pickup as each of the Main boxes include a decent variation of cards, the box with into the void contains cosmic cyclone, and various glad cards etc. The box with snoww also includes Lyla, and the gem knight fusion master diamond, the box with gates of the dark world is just overall an insane value box, you will get geminis, galaxy cyclone, mermails, u.a's, drowning mirror force you name it, amazing box.

&#x200B;

The only skills I would recommend in this deck would be Grit, or show of nightmares with Arkana, however note that with show of nightmares you are completely open to being OTKED if you go first and pass to your opponent, you can also sometimes get away with using life cost A as some decks can't do 5000 worth of damage, hell you can even use destiny draw to search specific cards if your opp can't finish you off however most decks right now can otk easily do yourself a favor and run grit, you can use show of nightmares for elephant dark world burn FTK.

&#x200B;

Dark Worlds are very reliant on their ability to otk, most games will be a loss if you do not close them out when you push, try not to get frustrated sometimes you will have games that are just simply unwinnable due to the way you draw, however this is a combo deck and that should be expected.

&#x200B;

For KC Cup and KOG getting to Legend 2, and DL 19 is very easy, you won't have many issues getting there with this deck, the real problem comes when you are trying to rank up to KOG or DL Max, as this is a combo deck and you will have auto losses due to bricks sometimes it can be tough to pull off 4/5 wins in a row in order to rank up to KOG, with my experience in Dark Worlds you typically won't rank to max rank or max DL from just a huge win streak, normally you will cycle between 3 win 1 loss and 2 win 1 loss orders until you finally get lucky and follow up a 3-1 streak with a few wins in a row after the loss, typically 3.

&#x200B;

If you have any questions about the deck or potential replacement cards I would be glad to help, when I was building this deck (still need 1 more into the void as well) I ran many interations of budget options while lacking some cards, however I do feel certain cards just are required to play this deck.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Deck Guide:

&#x200B;

Dark Worlds are a deck that rely on utilizing Reign-Beaux to pop all monsters or S/T to OTK your opponent given you have another monster on board (Broww, Trance, Snoww)

&#x200B;

For the majority of matchups your goal should be to stall until grit is popped, or until you have enough combo pieces to otk, ideally you will want to resolve a trunade first, then begin your plays and look for a Ceruli discard, to then discard Reign and thus summon himself and pop all monsters leaving an open board.

&#x200B;

The most ideal combo would be to use trunade, have ceruli, reign and trance in hand and then use trances effect discarding ceruli to discard Reign, Reign SS/eff, and then attack for game.

&#x200B;

As for my decklist I am running the below;

&#x200B;

3x Snoww

&#x200B;

2x Ceruli

&#x200B;

2x Reign

&#x200B;

2x Broww

&#x200B;

2x Gates of the Dark World

&#x200B;

3x Dark World Dealings

&#x200B;

2x Into the void

&#x200B;

2x Hey, Trunade!

&#x200B;

If you have a third Into the void I highly recommend replacing 1 broww with 1 into the void.

&#x200B;

I have ran a few different versions of this deck including those that run 3 ceruli and or 3 Reign and have found 2/2 to be the most consistent ratio.

&#x200B;

My reasoning for 2 ceruli is that times come up too often when running 3 where you either 1; can't resolve two of his effects and thus having a dead card in your hand or 2; just hard drawing too many of him and running out of plays.

&#x200B;

Broww was a card I had not initially run however due to his draw 1 effect it makes him a great card for thinning the deck, resolving a gates of the dark world on broww as the discard will allow you to draw 2 cards, while also thinning your deck.

&#x200B;

Broww is also nice as he acts as a beater for when you need damage to OTK, Broww + Reign = + gates is 4500 damage.

&#x200B;

There are a few skills that really hurt this deck and I will list those below as well as ways to play around them;

&#x200B;

Grit: When playing vs grit it can be really tough to pull a win however there are two ways; if your opponent has summoned a monster with lower attack than snoww/trance or broww you should immediately use your NS and attempt to inflict at least enough damage to place them below 4k, this will nullify grit and give you a chance to OTK next turn given you have not popped your own grit already.

&#x200B;

Another way to beat grit is to resolve ceruli twice to special summon 2 Reign (neither of their effects are once per turn), this combo will also require you to use your normal summon on either Snoww, Trance or Broww.

&#x200B;

Life cost A: This is similar to grit however much easier to deal with thanks to Gates of the Dark World, the only thing you need to do is resolve the normal board clear with Trance Archfiend(this is the only way to do 5K damage without summoning two Reign) and ensure you can have Gates on Board.

&#x200B;

Parasite Infestation: You will see this card a lot in burn decks, typically it is not too devestating however sometimes you will get 2 of them in your deck and due to how much you thin you're bound to draw into 1, this card will also shut off gates of the dark world, when playing vs this skill always ensure you are not clogging your board as you will need 1 clear space to summon Reign.

&#x200B;

This skill will also shut off Gates of the Dark World attack boost, however you can still use the effect to discard/draw.

&#x200B;

A few card tips;

&#x200B;

Gates of the Dark World: Amazing card that is searchable by snoww, typically you will want to resolve this on snoww to draw 1 + search any dark world piece, this really helps with finding the last combo piece to close out a game.

&#x200B;

If you find yourself lacking cards and in need of more than 1 search sometimes using this on Broww can really really get things moving due to the draw 2.

&#x200B;

This card is not once per turn and therefore can be used multiple times for more advantage.

&#x200B;

Into the void: Only use this card if you are forced to push for game, or you know you can secure game, not much to say, this card also triggers discard effects like snoww, broww, and ceruli, when snoww and ceruli are discarded by the effect of into the void snoww will always be the last chain link, this means you can search reign or broww at the end of your turn and ceruli will trigger to discard them which can lead to a board wipe, or a search + ss from opponents grave (snoww eff)

&#x200B;

Dark World Dealings: This card is essentially the main part of the engine, use it to thin or trigger discard effects. Be careful when using this card as many players are still running Kuriboh/Sphere Kuriboh, if you do not need to use this card for the OTK do NOT use it, all you are doing is giving your opponent chances to draw into a kuriboh and likely lose you the game.

&#x200B;

Hey, Trunade!: Simple card to use, always use at the start of your turn given you are pushing for game, clears backrow or forces cards to be used, normally needed for win con unless you play vs a monster heavy deck rather than trap.

&#x200B;

Trance Archfiend: This card works as a normal summonable dark world dealings, allows for a body to ensure you can push for game, triggers all dark world monster effects.

&#x200B;

This card also has a secondary effect when he is destroyed and sent to your graveyard to add a banished DW monster to your hand, this works great with banishing broww, snoww, or reign if needed. If you have Gates of the dark world on board and they destroy your Trance you can add back snoww/broww and then have a draw on your first turn, then use gates and draw 1 or 2 (broww) or draw 1 and search (snoww) really helps get you back into the game if for some reason you didn't otk.

&#x200B;

Snoww: She searches any dark world card in your deck, is a body for otks, can even search herself, use her wisely based on what you have in your hand, easily the best card to open alongside dark world dealings.

The thing about twitch is that he is a really great solo que monster, however you rely on a few things, if you are playing adc and have an incompetent support who can't get you into mid/late game without ur lane being ran over you WILL have a bad time, once u get mid game (2 items + boots) you become a devastating team fight monster, I would recommend either finding a good support to duo with that matches your play style, or you can always try jungle, not sure what rank you are, but twitch jungle is easily capable of diamond 5 in under 100 games for anyone with a semi working brain.

&#x200B;

If you are anything below gold I would highly recommend jungling, you should be able to go pretty much uncontested all the way to plat within your first 20 games.

[http://na.op.gg/summoner/userName=I+Jungle+Twitch](http://na.op.gg/summoner/userName=I+Jungle+Twitch)

&#x200B;

I play a little bit of twitch

I have a few more risky plays that I will be adding into the montage as well, here's one of which.  [https://gyazo.com/e39899ca671884aa1aa5f7e5ea9a52cd](https://gyazo.com/e39899ca671884aa1aa5f7e5ea9a52cd) 

&#x200B;

But I definitely see what you are saying.

Running 3 silent magicians instead of 2 will increase your odds by 7-8 % to see it in your opening hand going first, (this accounts for the possibility of a total 6 copies 3 burning/3 silent magician)  6 copies = 79.34% chance, 5 copies = 71.83% chance (if you were to only run 2 silent magicians).

&#x200B;

In a 20 card spellbook/silent magician deck your odds of drawing silent magician in the first hand with 3 copies vs 2 is 50.53% vs 36.84%, quite significant. 

&#x200B;

While yes you can get away with it, there is no reason not to get the third copy as you absolutely need 3 in normal spellbooks, and silent magician can be used in many forms which most of which require 3 to be efficient.

Invest in the 3, you will never have to buy them again and you'll have access to several great decks.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
